verdicts.corrected_claim:
Real but unpriced. In shadow rasters, three's shared _depthMaterial and the shared swayDepthMaterial re-resolve programs on every switch between batched, instanced and plain casters, and on every crossing of sway alphaTest 0↔>0, because candidates arrive in DFS order.

Fixes, pixel-identical:
- stable-sort candidates by depth-program kind;
- use two sway depth materials (cutout and solid);
- add a needsProgramChange counter, so it can be priced on the laptop first.

The estimated gain is about 0.3-2 ms per full raster. Ignore the 31 µs vs colour-draw argument.

