findings.evidence:
Order in tickPerFrame: loop.js:3041 tickCellVisibility3D (CRITICAL #1), then :3063 tickFrustumCull (#1.5), then :3423 cameraSwitcher.tick (#13). camera.js positionCamera only calls lookAt (camera.js:1120), so the camera's matrixWorldInverse refreshes inside renderer.render.

The MVPs are built from camera.matrixWorldInverse at culling.js:166 and cells.js:3123, i.e. the previous frame's view. So these appear one frame late at the leading edge of a turn (BatchedMesh statics and buildings are unaffected, because three culls them per instance with the live camera):
- interior/dungeon cells and rooms behind doorways (getRenderSetWithFrustum/PView, cells.js:3137-3157; cells-pass narrowing when split-armed);
- singleton Mesh/LOD statics with tight spheres (statics.js:4647+);
- entity roots beyond ~60 m (6 m sphere, entities.js:3075, 3248-3250).

Scale: about 3.6° per frame at a 180°/s flick at 50 fps, roughly a 4% band of the 84° horizontal FOV.

