findings.evidence:
luminous_night.js:22-34 explains the trap: three's Material.copy JSON-copies userData, so a clone carries `hbLumBase`, registerLuminousMaterial refuses it (luminous_night.js:106-111), and its glow freezes at the scale live when it was cloned. adoptLuminousClone (luminous_night.js:125-138) fixes this, but it is called only for per-entity clones (entities.js:15120, :15153).

The four cache variants clone the registered base and never adopt:
- getCachedFloorBias (materials.js:4078-4091; every building shell surface);
- getCachedCellBaked (:4110-4123; EnvCell walls);
- getCachedStaticBias (:4158-4170; cell décor);
- getCachedVariant (:4188-4206), which frag_install uses for every frag-plan model, including the windSwayGpu variant on wind-responsive foliage (vfx/frag_attach.js:80-88; 404 tipFlex + 103 windBend descriptors in visual_descriptors.jsonl).

Batched variants mirror emissiveIntensity from the member (luminous_night.js:20-21), and here the member is the stale clone. The canopies lumNight was built for (L=0.5, 0x08000AB1/0x08000E23, luminous_night.js:8-13) are tree surfaces, so a session that crosses day and night shows them at the clone-time brightness (neon at night if baked at noon, or 4x dim by day). Eye tests at a pinned sky time cannot see it.

